Subject: [PATCH] facetimehd: bound interrupt service and quiesce a stuck ISP

The IRQ retry loop reuses its counter while scanning firmware channels.
A latched source can keep the worker running indefinitely and block
cancel_work_sync() on suspend. Ring delivery can also run indefinitely
if the firmware refills a channel or the driver cannot reply to a slot.

Service one interrupt snapshot per work item. Give each active channel
a bounded turn and remember unfinished channels after acknowledging the
ISP. Count consecutive failed acknowledgements without ring progress on
each source separately. Recheck status when rearming and mask the device
on a fault. Keep the shared handler registered until teardown and wait
for the worker before releasing its resources.

